                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "150ce7f9-5f0f-411a-900f-64bbc812bf34",
                                                "sense_id": "d65ea953-3577-3668-9908-5a415735842b",
                                                "text": "Pro. Then, as my gueſt, and thine owne acquiſition / Worthily purchas'd, take my daughter : But / If thou do'ſt breake her Virgin-knot, before / All ſanctimonious ceremonies may / With full and holy right, be miniſtred, / No ſweet aſperſion ſhall the heauens let fall / To make this contract grow; but barraine hate, / Sower-ey'd diſdaine, and diſcord ſhall beſtrew / The vnion of your bed, with weedes ſo loathly / That you ſhall hate it both : Therefore take heede, / As Hymens Lamps ſhall light you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2951726f-6ad7-4222-ada0-fd0b626f5134",
                                                "sense_id": "d65ea953-3577-3668-9908-5a415735842b",
                                                "text": "It is allowed, that Senates and great Councils are often troubled with redundant, ebullient, and other peccant Humours, with many Diſeaſes of the Head and more of the Heart; with ſtrong Convulſions, with grievous Contractions of the Nerves and Sinews in both Hands, but eſpecially the Right; with Spleen, Flatus, Vertigos and Deliriums; with Scrophulous Tumors full of fœtid purulent Matter; with ſower frothy Ructations, with Canine Appetites and Crudeneſs of Digeſtion, beſides many others needleſs to mention."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
